# Contracts

Vault must distinguish TVL, committed/allocated credit, and actual utilization.

`KredxoTradingAccount` controls capital. Traders cannot withdraw credit as unrestricted USDC.

`KredxoRiskPolicy` stores creditLimit, maxLeverage, dailyLossLimit, validFrom, validUntil, riskLevel, active, plus per-market position limits.

Only `KredxoRiskController` with `RISK_CONTROLLER_ROLE` may update policy. Trading reads the live policy, never a frontend cache.

Trade validation (all onchain): account active, market allowed, credit available, leverage allowed, position limit, daily loss limit. Over-limit trades must revert.

Phase 18 `ExecutionRouter` must not hold funds, must not execute arbitrary calldata, and may only call allowlisted adapters. Adapter 0 is this account. Next: Perpl, then Kuru. Aave is out of Phase 18.

Minimum vault interface: `deposit`, `withdraw`, `allocateCredit`, `releaseCredit`, `repay`.

Write Foundry tests for every new function before moving on. Access control, reentrancy, precision, stale/expired policies, and unauthorized allocation are blocking.
